मण्डलम् संयोजन ॥ ॰ samyojana — the port of crates/sadhana/src/samyojana.rs

॰ ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
॰ THE LINKER, task D-002b, doc 03 §8. It links from OBJECTS — bytes, a
॰ symbol table and a list of holes — not by re-encoding from source.
॰
॰ Applying a relocation is: decode the instruction, find its displacement
॰ or immediate slot, and place the value with the same code the encoder
॰ uses. Nothing here knows that a jal scatters its displacement across
॰ four discontiguous runs — the derived map knows, and the map was
॰ measured. That is why पदपुनर्निर्माणम् below calls सङ्केतन ॱ स्थापनम्
॰ rather than transcribing the J-type layout a second time.
॰
॰ ── ON THE NAMES THIS FILE IMPORTS ──
॰ वास्तु and कोश are named here in the spelling their HAND-PORT will
॰ carry. Both files are still tools/port_encode.py output today
॰ (मण्डलम् वअसतउ, मण्डलम् कओश), so those two names resolve to nothing
॰ yet. This is the convention पदविभाग and व्याकर already follow —
॰ व्याकर names वास्तुॱअभिव्यञ्जककोश, which वअसतउ does not define either.
॰ Writing the machine transliteration into a hand-written file would
॰ spread the mistake instead of leaving one file to fix.
॰
॰ ── WHAT IS NOT PORTED, AND WHY ── NOTHING IS, SINCE 2026-08-30. This note
॰ used to read "see the four stubs at the foot of the file; each returns
॰ अपूर्णम् and names the thing it waits on". All three blockers are
॰ discharged and each discharge is recorded at the foot rather than deleted,
॰ because two of the three were STALE: (b) named a decoder that vishlesana.t1
॰ already carries, and (c) named an allocator decision the language never
॰ needed — an arena here grows by being written past its end.
