सार्वजनिक चरः भारणस्थानम् ॱॱ न६४ भवति २१४७४८३६४८ ।

॰ where a definition was placed — वास्तु ॱ स्थापन PLUS ONE, and the offset is
॰ the point rather than a slip.
॰
॰ THIS MARGIN READ "mirrors वास्तु ॱ Placement" UNTIL 2026-09-07 AND THAT WAS
॰ FALSE. The गणना is ZERO-based — `पाठ्यम्` reads ०, as does Rust's
॰ `Placement::Text`, neither carrying explicit discriminants — and every
॰ constant below is one higher.
॰
॰ WHY THE OFFSET IS RIGHT: a fresh record is `भवति ०`, so `स्थापनम्` starts at
॰ ० before anything fills it. `स्थापनाधारः` below has arms for १ २ ३ and falls
॰ through to `शून्यम्`. With Text=० AN UNFILLED RECORD WOULD READ AS ॱपाठ and
॰ be placed at the text base; with Text=१ it is REFUSED. The numbering buys the
॰ distinction between UNSET and THE FIRST VARIANT, which is worth more than
॰ agreeing with the enum's ordinals.
॰
॰ AND THE TRAP THE OLD WORDING SET, which is why this is corrected rather than
॰ deleted: the obvious spelling for a writer who believes the old sentence is
॰ `संज्ञा ॱ स्थापनम् भवति वास्तुॱपाठ्यम्`. That yields ०, `स्थापनाधारः` answers
॰ `शून्यम्`, and THE SYMBOL SILENTLY GETS NO ADDRESS — it links and resolves
॰ nowhere. A margin that describes the intent inaccurately is worse than none,
॰ because the accurate-sounding version is what the next writer follows.
॰
॰ `t1_vastu_build.rs` pins each constant to its variant PLUS ONE. Not to the
॰ variant — that fails today — and not on its own, which nothing could refute.
॰ The change it is for is someone correcting the off-by-one in ONE place.
॰
॰ integers rather than a गणना for the same reason सङ्केतन mirrors
॰ RelSection as integers: the enum lives in another module and this file
॰ must be readable before that module is hand-ported.
