॰ one name and the absolute address it ended up at.
॰ Rust holds these in a BTreeMap<String, u64>; T1 has no map, so the
॰ pairs are a slice and स्थानान्वेषणम् below is the lookup. lossy by
॰ construction in both: two objects may each define a local चक्रः and
॰ only one entry survives — सारणी is the truth.
॰ नामसूचीकोश is the hash index of the TABLE the entry is in (symbol-lookup step
॰ 2): every entry of one table carries the same one, so a table answers its own
॰ lookups without a second parameter beside it. See `नामसूचीक्रमः`.
