॰
॰ THE NAMES BELOW ARE BUILT ONE OCTET AT A TIME, AND THAT IS FORCED. Rust
॰ writes kind_named("R_RISCV_JAL") and `name.as_str() == ".debug_info"`; T1
॰ HAS NO STRING LITERAL THAT CAN HOLD THEM. `उक्तम् … इति` exists — अर्थ:338
॰ compares against `उक्तम् अ३२ इति` — but its content is lexed as ordinary
॰ words, and every word must be in the doc 15 repertoire. `R` is not, and
॰ neither is `.`; a literal `उक्तम् R_RISCV_JAL इति` fails
॰ every_t1_source_lexes_and_parses with "`R` is outside the doc 15 repertoire".
॰ MEASURED, not assumed: that is the error this file produced when it was
॰ first written with the literals in it.
॰
॰ The idiom is वाक्यविभाग's own — दत्तक्षेत्रआज्ञाकूटः (vakyavibhaga.t1:915)
॰ is an `अङ्कः अन्तः अ८` filled with ८०, ४८, ४९, the octets of `P01`. These
॰ are ASCII, and ASCII is what the derived tables and DWARF are written in;
॰ the octet is the only thing about them this language can say.

॰ append one octet to a run — the one-octet half of अष्टकसंयोगः, so the
॰ spellings below read as a list of characters and not as an index walk.
