॰ write a value into the named field of the instruction at स्थानाङ्कः — patch.
॰
॰ THIS ANSWERS THE PATCHED RUN, where Rust writes through `text: &mut [u8]`
॰ and answers Result<(), String>. See the note above अष्टाष्टकनिधानम्: a T1
॰ routine cannot write into its caller's octets, so a बूल here would report
॰ success over bytes the caller does not have. शून्यम् is the refusal and the
॰ reason is appended to संयोजनदोषकोश.
॰
॰ भेदः IS A SLOT KIND IN सङ्केतन'S NUMBERING — सङ्केतनॱअन्तरभेद where Rust
॰ writes "disp", सङ्केतनॱतत्कालभेद where it writes "imm". That is not a
॰ translation choice made here: विश्लेषण already carries the kinds as
॰ numbers because T1 has no string equality, and one comparison has to serve
॰ both files.
॰
॰ ON READING FOUR OCTETS UNCONDITIONALLY, which is Rust's own long note:
॰ a relocation is only ever recorded for an instruction naming a symbol the
॰ file does not define, and सङ्केतन ॱ सङ्कोचः begins by encoding the wide
॰ form — which fails for exactly those. So an instruction carrying a
॰ relocation cannot have been compressed. IF A FUTURE LINKER RELAXES ACROSS
॰ OBJECTS that property dies and this silently re-encodes over two
॰ instructions; ask विश्लेषण ॱ आज्ञादैर्घ्यम् with that change, not after it.
॰ `W-359`: the run unchanged and `निधानविफलम्` raised where this answered
॰ `शून्यम्`; the tail call answers through `चतुरष्टकनिधानम्`, which sets the
॰ status itself — so this grows-and-returns `पाठ्यम्` by transitivity.
